# Dockerfile.dockerignore -- RAMEAU shell-MCP
#
# Named for the Dockerfile beside it, not `.dockerignore`. That naming is load-bearing: a
# plain `.dockerignore` here would sit outside the build context (which is
# services/shell-mcp/) and Docker would read it not at all.
#
# THE CONTEXT IS TWO FILES, so almost nothing here has work to do today, and that is the
# point rather than an argument for leaving it out. The never-block below is what stops a
# credential that appears in that directory later from reaching a published image, and the
# `images` job builds a planted context against this exact file and compares the transferred
# list, so these patterns are asserted rather than asserted-about.

# ---- build and editor droppings ----
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.log
**/*.bak
**/*.sqlite

# ---- never, under any circumstances ----
# Every pattern below is the floor in deploy/images/NEVER-BLOCK-SHAPES.txt, carried
# verbatim. The floor is a MINIMUM: a never-block may deny more. Do not reflow or
# re-order these lines -- tools/check_never_block_shapes.py compares them as text.

# --- environment and secrets ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/secrets/
**/.secrets/
**/*.secret
**/*.secrets
**/credentials.json
**/*credential*
**/*-credentials*
**/auth.json
**/.sops.yaml
**/.sops/
**/*.kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig.*

# --- keys and certificates ---
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa.*
**/id_ed25519
**/id_ed25519.*
**/*.ppk
**/known_hosts

# --- tokens ---
**/*.token
**/.netrc
**/_netrc
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc

# --- repository metadata, which carries remotes and credentials of its own ---
**/.git-credentials
**/.git/
**/.github/
